<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maréchal, nous voilà !</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Maréchal, nous voilà !&quot; (&quot;Marshal, here we are!&quot;) is a French propaganda song of 1941 in honour of Marshal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippe-petain">Philippe Pétain</a>, head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> regime, an authoritarian and antisemitic state set up during the German occupation.</p></div>
